  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "25",
  "quote": "A landlord may enter a rental unit only in accordance with section 26 or 27.",
  "reason": "Sections 25, 26, and 27 of the Act restrict a landlord's right to enter a rental unit, requiring 24 hours' written notice for routine inspections to determine if the unit is in a good state of repair unless the tenant consents at the time of entry. Because this clause purports to allow entry for inspections without advance written notice or consent at the time of entry, it conflicts with the Act and is void under subsection 4(1)."
}

